{# ── Chapter: Takeaway ── #}
<section class="case-chapter" data-chapter="takeaway">
  <h2>Remember</h2>
  <div class="case-takeaway">
    <h3>Key takeaways</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <div class="tone-junior">Env vars read at build time, Vite's import.meta.env, webpack's DefinePlugin, get inlined into the bundle permanently — the same build can't be promoted across staging and production without a rebuild.</div>
        <div class="tone-mid">A small config.json, or window-injected config, fetched at app boot lets one built artifact run correctly in any environment, because the environment-specific values live outside the bundle instead of inside it.</div>
        <div class="tone-staff">Runtime config has real costs: code that assumed synchronous access to env vars needs refactoring, and config.json needs to be fetched fresh every boot, never cached the way the rest of the build is.</div>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>
